// Watchdog for the "D-Code bug": when a per-room-member profile fetch wedges
// (state 6 payload-rejected, or a >15s state-2 stall), force the slot back to
// idle so the game's own retry path re-fetches. See docs/Research/DCodeNetworkStallBug.md.
SETTING(bool, dcodeAutoRecover, "DCodeAutoRecover", "1");
// TEST ONLY: sabotage the first in-flight profile fetch after launch (corrupts
// the receive buffer so the game's checksum rejects it) to exercise the state-6
// wedge + auto-recovery end-to-end. Fires once per launch while set to 1.
SETTING(bool, dcodeForceFailureOnce, "DCodeForceFailureOnce", "0");
// When the game latches its "network profile storage unavailable" flag (which
// silently stops uploading your profile, so ranked/net-color progress is lost on
// restart), reset it so uploads resume. See docs/Research/DCodeNetworkStallBug.md.
SETTING(bool, dcodeTusGateAutoClear, "DCodeTusGateAutoClear", "1");
// Spectator desync fix: when the spectator's SyncInput would report starvation
// (input not yet received over the network), substitutes the previous frame's real
// input instead of letting the game's caller advance the simulation with a fake
// zeroed input (the desync mechanism). Always active while spectatorSyncHooksEnabled
// is on -- there is no separate on/off toggle for the fix itself, since substitution
// is unconditionally safer than both the original bug and the retired "force stall"
// attempt (see docs/Research/SpectatorDesyncInvestigation.md for why that one
// crashed the game with a GGPO event-queue assertion, and why this design doesn't).
// Kill-switch for the spectator-sync hooks (SpectatorSyncInputEntry +
// SpectatorSyncStarvation). 1 = install as normal (default). 0 = don't install them
// at all, falling back to pure vanilla behavior (the original desync bug, unfixed).
// Read at startup only -- requires a restart to take effect either way.
SETTING(bool, spectatorSyncHooksEnabled, "SpectatorSyncHooksEnabled", "1");
// FPS-drop investigation (2026-08-02 Discord reports, unconfirmed as mod-caused):
// when enabled, measures real frame-to-frame time each match frame and, if a
// frame exceeds FrameStallThresholdMs, logs a breakdown of how much of that
// time was spent inside the mod's own EndScene hook code versus outside it
// (base game/driver/OS) to DEBUG.txt and BBCF_IM\FrameStallIncidents.log.
// See src/Game/FrameStallDiagnostics.h.
SETTING(bool, logFrameStalls, "LogFrameStalls", "0");
SETTING(int, frameStallThresholdMs, "FrameStallThresholdMs", "33");
// Fallback path for when another resident hooker owns d3d9's Direct3DCreate9Ex export and
// evicts our detour before the game creates its device (confirmed with NVIDIA Optimus'
// nvd3d9wrap.dll, which re-applies its own patch ~300ms after ours and drops us out of the
// call chain -- the overlay then never appears). The fallback hooks the game's IMPORT table
// entry instead of the export prologue, which nobody else contends for.
// 0 = Off (never; pure pre-8.3 behavior), 1 = Automatic (default; only when the export is
// already owned by a foreign module at startup, or after we observe our detour evicted),
// 2 = Always (install unconditionally; diagnostic use).
// On a machine where nothing contends for the export, Automatic does nothing at all.
// Enum options rendered by SettingsIniWindow.cpp's kSettingEnumMetadata.
// Read at startup only -- requires a restart to take effect.
SETTING(int, d3d9IatFallbackHook, "D3D9IatFallbackHook", "1");
// Force Platinum's personality/voice (Sena/Luna) for the Platinum YOU control: 0 = Default
// (vanilla RNG), 1 = force Luna, 2 = force Sena. Enum options rendered by
// SettingsIniWindow.cpp's kSettingEnumMetadata. Client-side audio-only override (hooks the
// voice-bank load + play resolvers in hooks_palette.cpp, never writes the game's checksummed
// select-struct field). OFFLINE ONLY: forced off in ONLINE matches (hooks_palette.cpp,
// PlatinumVoiceChoiceForSlot) pending investigation of a field-reported match desync that
// correlated with this override actually changing something online - see the block comment
// there for details. See docs/Research/PlatinumVoiceChoiceInvestigation.md for the full RE writeup.
SETTING(int, platinumVoiceChoice, "PlatinumVoiceChoice", "0");
// Keep the last N sessions' DEBUG.txt files in BBCF_IM\DebugHistory (rotated at
// launch). 0 = old behavior, DEBUG.txt is overwritten every launch.
SETTING(int, debugLogSessionHistory, "DebugLogSessionHistory", "10");
